+## Deliberate reversal, exclusive touch and tab outlines (2026-10-04)
+
+Requirements **R01/V03/V04/V05/Q01**. The owner reports that back-and-forth swiping sometimes changes pages and asks to remove the yellow outline that remains on the last tapped tab after a swipe. This follows the held Create-biome-card release complaint above.
+
+Page-change intent still arms after **20 logical units**. An actual backward MOVE of **20 units from the stroke's furthest position** now cancels it, including when the finger remains far from the original press. Returning within six units or crossing the origin also clears that direction. A new 20-unit forward stroke from the reversal's trough can rearm it; a tiny forward UP cannot. Small relaxation remains accepted: the existing 20-to-eight-unit test still commits. Stationary holds have no timeout. Canceled movement uses the existing shared smootherstep return from the exact displayed position, keeping both pages and their gutter together.
+
+Full-engine dispatch with an explicit parallel real-mouse DOWN/UP stream exposes another input path: the mouse release activates the moving biome card before touch UP, rebuilding Create and losing the swipe. The previous emulation-only guard fails four checks across two viewport sizes. While page navigation owns a touch, **all parallel mouse events** are now consumed. The moving body's native mouse/focus subtree gate also prevents its controls from acting during drag/return and restores them on completion, cancellation, zero-offset release or a new press. Ordinary desktop mouse, single touch taps, inner carousel/range/editor input and modal ownership remain covered. The identity of any additional native mouse stream in the owner's original physical gesture was not instrumented; this is a reproduced failure path and defensive correction, not proof of that device event identity.
+
+Primary Race/Create/Garage tabs now override the focus style with an empty box. Their actual selected-page background/text continue to update, and the last tapped tab no longer retains a yellow focus rectangle after swiping. Fixed navigation, live neighboring content, 64-unit gutter and outer-end spring are retained. No simulation/rules/schema/backend/ad change.
+
+Changed files: `game/ui/menu_page_swipe.gd` (input exclusivity/reversal tracking), `game/core/app.gd` (moving-body input gate/restore and tab focus style), `game/tests/test_menu_page_swipe.gd` (parallel-input, repeated reversal, fresh-stroke rearm and interaction restoration), this document, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md`, `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md` and `docs/evidence/exclusive-menu-swipes-2026-10-04/`. Concurrent menu-quality/loading/account/backend work is preserved; the scoped before/after patch contains this task's edits only. No mixed-workspace commit.
